        <p>A CIRCUIT RECOGNITION MEETING WII L BE HELD IN THE BOLD STREET WESLEYAN CHURCH, ON THURSDAY NEXT, SEPTEMBER 7TH, 1911, TO WELCOME THE NEWLY-APPOINTED NIIN LEITERS. THE REV. W. A. BECKETT. REV. E. MORGAN. REV. H. WILLIAMSON, B.A. REV. H. lIIDDLBWOOD. REV. W. NICHOLSON.</p>
        <p>SERVICES IN THE AFTERNOON AT 4.30. PREACHER: THE REV. W. A. BECKETT. TEA IN SCHOOLROOM AT 5.30. TICKETS 60. EACH. PUBLIC MEETING IN THE CHURCH AT 710. SPECIAL MUSIC BY THE CHOIR. F. A. HARRIS, EN., CIRCUIT STEWARD, • WILL PRESIDE. COLLECTIONS FOR CIRCUIT EXPENSES. ROYAL COURT THEATRE WARRINGTON. PRormt.ron : Ms. JOSEPH BEECHAM. Guseso. MAsAGEn Mn. A. M. LOADER. ACTING MANAGER: MR. H. WARBURTON. MONDAY, SEPTEMBER 470., 1911, AND FITZ FOLLOWING NIGHTS. MR. JAMES WELCH'S COMPANY IN 1. WHEN KNIGHTS WERE BOLD." By CHARLES :MARLOWE. (The Great West End success from Wyndham's Theatre.) THE LONGEST RUN OF THE CENTURY. SMOKING PERMITTED. PRICES OF ADMISSION: Booked or Late Early Late early door, door, door. door. 2s. 6d. 2s. Pit Id. 6d. 2s. Is. 6d.</p>
        <p>Stalls : First three rovrs</p>
