        <p>Grand Irle First two rows 2s. 6d. 2s. Gallery 6d. 4d. Other rows is. td. Is. Private boxes (to seat three). 10a. 6d. Early doors open 7 o'clock. Ordinary door, 7.15. Commence 7.30. Half-price at 8.45. BRITISH WOMEN'S TEMPERANCE ASSOCIATION.—REV. R. PATTERSON, LLB., author of the " Catch-my-Pal" movement, will be in Warrington on Wednesday evening Nov. let. The monthly meeting will bs held next Wednesday, Sep. Btb, at 3 in the Chinch Parloitr, Bold-street. COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.— EDUCATION. COMMITTEE.</p>
        <p>SCHOOL OF ART. THE DAY AND EVENING CLASSES RE-OPEN ON MONDAY, THE 11"ffit SEPTEMBER, lEil. Intending at ucteuts should consult the Headmaster at the School. Prospectuses and further particulars may be obtained from him and from J. MOORE MURRAY, M. Sc., Secretary and Director. Education Office, Sankey Street, August, 1911. W ARRINGTON UNION.— PROBATIONER NURSES.</p>
        <p>Applicatiors are invited from Single WOO7OO, or Widows, for the appointment of TWO PROBKIIONER NURSES at the Union Infirmary. Salary first year £9, second year £l2, third year £l5, together with Apartments, Retinas, Wasting, Indoor Uniform, end Medical Attendance in aickness whilst In the Hospital. Forms of application can be obtained from the under- signed, and the application forms must be filled up in the candidates own writing, and returned to me not later than loam, on Thursday the 14th September, 1911. e By older, ARTHUR BOTTOIILEY, Clerk. Bewsey Chambers, Warrington, August 20th, 1911. TO CLOSE A T-111:11ST. VALUABLE FREEHOLD LAND AND PROPERTY</p>
        <p>AT RUNCORN. TO BE SOLD BY AUCTION BY MR. FRANK HICKMAN.</p>
