        <p>GEDDES'S DANDELION COFFEE. THE BEST AND CHEAPEST EVER OFFERED TO THE PUBLIC. BOLD BY ALL GROCERS AND DRUGGISTS IN CANISTERS SD., lOD., AND 18. BD. EACH. WHOLISALN BY 3. MINAS &amp; SON LTD. WARRINGTON</p>
        <p>B. (:)lINNDIGHAM, 29, FROGHALL LANE, %ARRINGTON. BREWER'S AGENT AND BOTTLER OF Guinness's Stout, Bass's Pale Ale, Sass's No. 1 Strong Ale. Worthington's and Allsopp's Ales. Devonshire and Hereford Cider. Wheatley's and Mack's Hop Bitters. Allsopp's and Jeffrey's LAGER BEIER IN BOTTLN. ALSO MANIIPACTURIRS Or 1113 H-CLASS MINERAL WATERS. Telephowe 79. IN THE MATTER OF THE COMPANIES (CONSOLIDATION) ACT, 1908, AND IN THE MATTER OF THE S TRETTON, WHITLEY AND DISTRICT MOTOR BUS COMPANY, LIMITED. (IN VOLUNTARY LIQUIDAIION). TE CREDITORS OF THE ABOVE-NAMED COMPANY, which is being voluntarily wound up, are required, on or before the 2nd day of Ootober, 1911, to send in their names and addressee ank parti- culars of their debts or claims, and the names end addresses of their Solicitors (if any), to JOHN GREEN CHAPPELL of No. 11, Mill Street, Warrington, the i liquidator of the said Company ; and, fno required by notice in writing from the said liquidator, are, by their Solicitors, or personally, to come in and prove their debts or claims, at such time ani place as shall be specified in such notice, or in default thereof they will be excluded from the benefit of any distribution made before such debts are proved. Dated this Thirty-fist day of August, 1911. J. GREEN CHAPPELL, Liquidator. WARRING-TON UNION DYNAMOS FOR SALE.</p>
        <p>The GUARDIANS of this Union have for sale TWO STEAM DYNAMOS, each consisting of an Alley and McLellan Sentinel Type Campoun4 non-candensing Engine working at 475 revolutions per minute, capable of developing 62 H.P. at a working pressure of 1251b5. of steam per square inch, each coupled direct to a 2-pole shunt wound Dynamo fitted on an extension of the engine soleplate, the capacity of the Dynamo being 180 Amperes 220 volts. The Booster consists of a 12 H.P. Motor working on a 220 volts, circuit, coupled direct to a Dynamo generating 100-Amperes at 70 volts, running at a speed of 1100 revolutions per minute, the two machines being built on one soleplate. The Dynamos are Reed at the Union Workhouse, Warrington, and may be inspected on application being made to the Workhouse Master. Sealed Tenders endorsed " Dynamos " must reach me not later than Tuesday, 12th September, 1011.</p>
        <p>By order, Bewsey Members, AriTliUß BOTTOMLEY, Werriottee 31st Aueust, 1911. Clerk.</p>
        <p>LANGLANDS RAILINGS to GREENOCK and GLASGOW. " PRINCESS LOUISE " or other STEAMER From LIVERPOOL From GLASGOW. (Clarence dock). (lteal's Nos. 22-28 North side) Sat. Sep. 2,5 p.m. Tues. Sept. 5,3 p.m. *9.30 p.m Thurs. Sept. 7,9 p.m. Sat. Sept. 9,3 p.m. *9.30 p.m. Toes. Sept 12,12 noon Thurs. Sept 14,3 p.m.* 7.10 p.m. *Train from Glasgow (Central) to Greenock (Central) SPECIAL REDUCED THROUGH TICKETS from Warringtoo, &amp;o. Single, tat class &amp; saloon 13..104. ; 3rd close &amp; saloon 12e. 64.; led class &amp; steerage 75. Return (valid for two mont)s, 3rd class &amp; *Moon 19s. SPECIAL 10 DAYS EXCURSION TICI:E IS : led class &amp; saloon 16s. Id. :3rd class &amp; steerage On. 64. M. LANGLANDS &amp; SUNS,</p>
        <p>_ 14, CROSS STREET, MANCHESTER. BROWN'S BUILDINGS, EXCHANGE. LIV ERPOOL -r IVERPOOL AND NORTH WALES 14 REGULAR DAILY SAILINGS (SUNDAYS included). 10 45 a.m. every Day, by" La Marguerite "for Llandudno (4 hours ashore), Beaumsris, Bangor and Menai Bridge, due hack in Liverpool 7.15 p m. 2.15 p.m Extra Sailing., on Friday Ist, Saturday 2nd and Mon- day 4th. 9.15 a.m. Isle of Anglesey Trips: Thursdsy 31st, and Sunday 3rd September. bor Train Bookings apply at station. For all further information and Conditions of Carriage apply to the Liverpool and North Wales Steamship Company, Ltd., T.G. BREW, Secretary, 40, Chapel at.. Liverpool. DUBLIN v. ALSO ENGLISH LAKES _ WHITEHAVEN.</p>
        <p>-Tit/CASTLE LINE. S.S. "BLACKROCK," " CUMBRIA," " end" ADELA," from SOUTH Side, NELSON DOCK, Liverpool. Every Tuesday, Wednesday, Friday and Saturday, to DUBLIN. Return Saloon, 10a.; Steerage ss. with Cheap Excursion Tickets EVERY SAILING, DAY, to Bray, Wicklow, Avoca, Au., and on Fridays and Saturdays to Killarney,Cork,Bundoran, Warrenpoint,Ao. Feat S.S. BLACEROCK" every Tuesday and Friday from Liverpool, and Mondays and Wednesdays from Dublin. SPECIAL SIX DAYS' SEA CRUISE, per "Cumbria." Every Saturday, to Wbitehaven, giving 3 days for English Lakes, thence to Dublin, and back to Liverpool (6 clays, or within 2 months). Saloon 225. 6d, or with 14 meals, 21s. additional. I Apply TEDCASTLE, McCORMICK ft CO., LTD Liverpool. Telegrams " Tedcastle." Telephone 975</p>
