      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-09-02_WidnesExaminer_art0022" n="art0022">
        <head>WARWICKSHIRE TEAM.</head>
        <p>THE WARWICKSHIRE TEAM.</p>
        <p>With the defeat of Northants this week Warwickshire have gained their first county championship. Warwickshire's rise in the cricket world is the most striking feature of the season's cricket. The credit of this is due to their youthful but able captain, Mr. F. R. Foster, who has imparted to the team that vim and energy necessary for such a brilliant achievement. Our photograph shows the team at Northampton. The names from left to right are : (back row) Charles- worth, Baker, —, Field, Parsons, Santa% Smith; (seated) Quaife, F. G. Stechens. F. R. Foster, G. W. Stephens, W. C. Han&amp;</p>
      </div>
