      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-09-02_WidnesExaminer_art0034" n="art0034">
        <head>WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT SUNDAY SCHOOL UNION</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT SUNDAY SCHOOL UNION</p>
        <p>It is not usnal during the summer to make such bead- Ivey with the organising of a new movement, tut it is quite evident from the progress that bee been made in the formation of a local Sunday School Colon for the Free Church Sunday Schools, that such an organization , was greatly needed. Since the gathering of Sunday school teachers bell in May, when Mr. A. Black, secretary of Liverpool Sunday School 'Union explained the aims of a Sunday School Union, the Provisional Committee then formed ban met on four occasions , and now th 3 Union has been formed on a arm basis. A constitution L. been drawn up and most of the sehools have applied for The following offices have been filled President, Rev William Reid; vice.preiidente. Rev 3 Youge, Alderman A Bennett. 12 mucillor J SAelland, Mr til Thornton, J.P., Mr Arthur klocnieht Mr 8 Fernley; secretaries, Miss Venda M Taylor and Mr Osborne Sinclair ' • treasurer, Mr F T Light. Arrangements hone been andel lir aTeschers Training Class, conducted by Bev William Reid, to commenco on October 12th, and furl coarse of lectures on "Child Training," by Ur. H. Thiseltha Mark, MA., Master of Method, Victoria University. Miss Janet Dewar and Mr. Lewsey bare been appoinied to represent the Union Et the !grout Confer- ence of Sunday school workers, to be held in the Central Hall, Liverpool, on September 2lst, whoa Mr. Marion Lowreene, the well-known Sunday school !alder of America, will be the principal speaker.</p>
