        <head>LOCAL PRESS AND DOAN'S.</head>
        <p>THE LOCAL PRESS AND DOAN'S.</p>
        <p>Important Step.</p>
        <p>The publication in the local press, of instances of men and women in the neighbourhood having been cured of kidney and bladder disorders by loan's back- ache kidney pills, has awakened such widespread interest that we have commissioned one of our repre- sentatives to investigate them, and to ascertain whether the cures have proved lasting. To-day wo give the evidence of a Warrington woman. Mrs. L. Selby, of 32, Devonshire Place, Tholwall- lane, Warrington, says :—" I was so ill with kidney complaint for five years that I did not know what to do for the best. Many a time I have been doubled up with the pains around my loins, and I did not know how to straighten myself. My head ached no badly at times that I could hardly see. The doctor told me that I was suffering from tidoey disease, but I got no better under his treatment, " Hearing of the good many people were getting from loan's backache kidney pills I got some to try. I can truthfully say that I am now quite cured. The pills did men world of good from the first, and I am glad I persevered with them and gave them a fair trial. They took away all the pains and removed the swellings I had in my feet, which bad been no bad that I could hardly stand. *I shall always speak well of Doan's pills. (Signed) (Mrs.) L. Selby.* Over 5 years after her care, Mrs. Selby raid :--e It is five years sinoe I gave my testimony for loan's pills. I have bad no kidney trouble since, and I am still well to-day. I have told many people how Donna pills I oared me." 2/9 is box, 6 boxes 13/9. Of all dcalere. Ask for DOAN'S Backache liidney Pills, like Mrs. Selby had.</p>
        <p>Doan'</p>
